---
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Paths from '../components/Paths.astro';
import Install from '../components/Install.astro';
import Snippet from '../components/Snippet.astro';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import {href} from '../site';
import duplicate from '../snippets/duplicate.ansi?raw';
import hello from '../snippets/hello.vun?raw';
import targets from '../snippets/targets.ansi?raw';
import '../styles/landing.css';

const paths = [
  {path: 'docs/', name: 'Read the docs', text: 'Install it, write a first program, then the commands, packages and targets.'},
  {path: 'docs/learn/', name: 'Take the course', text: 'Short lessons. Fix a program in the browser until its checks pass.'},
  {path: 'play/', name: 'Open the playground', text: 'Compile and run anything you paste, then share it as a link.'},
];
---

<Page title="vun" description="A smol systems programming language." bodyClass="landing">
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="logo" data-logo></div>
      <p class="tagline">a smol systems programming language :3</p>
      <p class="pitch">For code that runs under constraints: firmware, kernels, runtimes, servers.</p>
      <Install />
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href={href('docs/first-program/')}>Write a first program</a>
        <a class="button" href={href('play/')}>Try it in the browser</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="point">
      <div class="words">
        <h2>A program asks for what it uses</h2>
        <p><code>main</code> is handed <code>sys</code>, its way out to the world. Printing means asking <code>sys</code> for standard output, so a function that is not given it cannot print, open a file or reach the network.</p>
        <p>Nothing else is special either. The runtime is a function you call with your <code>main</code>, and the standard library has no powers your code lacks.</p>
      </div>
      <Snippet code={hello} lang="vun" title="main.vun" />
    </section>

    <section class="point flip">
      <div class="words">
        <h2>Errors have ids, places and fixes</h2>
        <p>Every diagnostic carries a stable id and points into your source. <code>vun explain names.duplicate</code> prints its page, <code>vun fix</code> applies the fixes that exist, and <code>--format json</code> gives a program the same records as lines of JSON.</p>
      </div>
      <Snippet code={duplicate} lang="ansi" title="vun check" />
    </section>

    <section class="point">
      <div class="words">
        <h2>One binary, many targets</h2>
        <p>A target is a path such as <code>bare.thumbv7em.eabihf</code>. <code>vun target list</code> shows what builds for each and what your machine lacks, a cross compiler or an emulator.</p>
        <p>Linux, macOS, Windows, WASI and Arm and RISC-V microcontrollers are on the list today.</p>
      </div>
      <Snippet code={targets} lang="ansi" title="vun target list" />
    </section>

    <section class="paths-section">
      <h2>Where to go next</h2>
      <Paths entries={paths.map((entry) => ({...entry, href: href(entry.path)}))} />
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Page>

<script>
  import {hero} from '../hero';
  void hero(document.querySelector('[data-logo]') as HTMLElement);
</script>
